d treatment: Case reviews of del(5q) patients with unexpected responses</article-title><source>Ann Hematol</source><year>2006</year><comment>in press</comment></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giagounidis</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Germing</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Haase</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clinical, morphological, cytogenetic, and prognostic features of patients with myelodysplastic syndromes and del(5q) including band q31</article-title><source>Leukemia</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14586479</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giagounidis</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Germing</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Strupp</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prognosis of patients with del(5q) MDS and complex karyotype and the possible role of lenalidomide in this patient subgroup</article-title><source>Ann Hematol</source><year>2005</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>569</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15891887</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giagounidis</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Germing</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Wainscoat</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The 5q- syndrome</article-title><source>Hematology</source><year>2004</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15621734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-